<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wilhelm Solf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1862">1862</a>–<a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wilhelm Solf was a German colonial administrator and diplomat. As the first governor of German Samoa from 1900 to 1911, he ruled through Samoan chiefs, limited land sales and suppressed opposition such as the Mau a Pule. He then served as colonial secretary until 1918, briefly as foreign secretary, and later as ambassador to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wilhelm-solf.jpg" alt="Wilhelm Solf" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R73059,_Wilhelm_Solf.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
